+# Offline exclusive-TTY candidate checks
+
+These checks use fresh PTYs under bubblewrap with private PID, network and
+device namespaces. They do not use a physical serial device or the running ROS
+master. The test-only `LD_PRELOAD` injector must never be loaded into a real
+driver process.
+
+From `/home/agilex/rosclaw/jev/worktrees/limo-driver`, build the isolated
+candidate in a new workspace (do not overwrite an existing path):
+
+```bash
+(
+set -e
+test ! -e /tmp/rosclaw-limo-exclusive-candidate
+mkdir -p /tmp/rosclaw-limo-exclusive-candidate/src
+ln -s "$PWD/limo_base" /tmp/rosclaw-limo-exclusive-candidate/src/limo_base
+source /opt/ros/melodic/setup.bash
+PATH=/usr/bin:/bin:/opt/ros/melodic/bin:$PATH catkin_make \
+  -C /tmp/rosclaw-limo-exclusive-candidate --pkg limo_base \
+  -DPYTHON_EXECUTABLE=/usr/bin/python2 -j2
+)
+```
+
+Compile and run the serial class regression using only a fresh PTY:
+
+```bash
+mkdir -p /tmp/rosclaw-limo-exclusive-tests
+g++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Ilimo_base/include \
+  limo_base/test/test_serial_port_exclusive.cpp limo_base/src/serial_port.cpp \
+  -Wl,--wrap=ioctl -Wl,--wrap=tcgetattr -lutil \
+  -o /tmp/rosclaw-limo-exclusive-tests/serial_test
+env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin:/sbin bwrap --unshare-all \
+  --hostname limo-exclusive-pty-isolated --die-with-parent \
+  --ro-bind /usr /usr --ro-bind /bin /bin --ro-bind /lib /lib --ro-bind /sbin /sbin \
+  --proc /proc --dev /dev --tmpfs /tmp \
+  --ro-bind /tmp/rosclaw-limo-exclusive-tests/serial_test /tmp/serial_test \
+  --chdir /tmp /tmp/serial_test
+```
+
+Compile the test-only failure injector and run the real candidate against a
+private ROS master and two fresh PTYs:
+
+```bash
+gcc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -fPIC -shared \
+  limo_base/test/fail_tiocexcl.c -ldl \
+  -o /tmp/rosclaw-limo-exclusive-tests/fail_tiocexcl.so
+env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin:/sbin bwrap --unshare-all \
+  --hostname limo-exclusive-pty-isolated --die-with-parent \
+  --ro-bind /usr /usr --ro-bind /bin /bin --ro-bind /lib /lib --ro-bind /sbin /sbin \
+  --ro-bind /opt/ros/melodic /opt/ros/melodic --proc /proc --dev /dev --tmpfs /tmp \
+  --ro-bind /tmp/rosclaw-limo-exclusive-candidate /tmp/rosclaw-limo-exclusive-candidate \
+  --ro-bind /tmp/rosclaw-limo-exclusive-tests/fail_tiocexcl.so /tmp/fail_tiocexcl.so \
+  --ro-bind "$PWD/limo_base/test" /sandbox --dir /etc \
+  --ro-bind /etc/hosts /etc/hosts --ro-bind /etc/nsswitch.conf /etc/nsswitch.conf \
+  --ro-bind /etc/passwd /etc/passwd --ro-bind /etc/group /etc/group \
+  --chdir /tmp --setenv ROS_HOME /tmp/ros-home --setenv PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE 1 \
+  /usr/bin/python3 /sandbox/test_driver_exclusive_pty.py
+```
+
+The class tests cover default nonexclusive opens, exclusion of later opens,
+continued use of a previously opened descriptor, normal and destructor release,
+duplicate opens, error handling, and fd closure on injected ioctl/termios
+failure. The driver test checks the default watchdog-off behavior, watchdog-on
+second-open denial and second-driver rejection, and verifies injected
+`TIOCEXCL` failure aborts before the candidate sends an initialization frame.
+
+`TIOCEXCL` does not revoke a descriptor opened before the ioctl, can be bypassed
+by a process with `CAP_SYS_ADMIN`, and has an open-to-ioctl race. A preexisting
+holder can also affect the terminal's global exclusive flag. Normal class close
+attempts `TIOCNXCL` before closing; abrupt termination cannot run that cleanup,
+and an existing PTY master/slave or other holder may keep the kernel flag alive
+until the last handle closes. Failure to clear the flag is reported on normal
+close; these checks do not establish absolute ownership or physical safety.
